{"availability":"available","full":"Chemaclass/agnostic-ai","name":"agnostic-ai","description":"One source to rule them all: write agents, skills, rules, and hooks once, then sync them to your AI tools.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":25,"forks":5,"created":"2026-05-03T18:47:55Z","updated":"2026-10-15T12:58:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://agnostic-ai.org","topics":["agentic-ai","agents-md","agnostic-ai","ai-agents","claude","claude-code","cli","codex","copilot","cursor","developer-tools","gemini","golang","mcp"],"demo":"https://agnostic-ai.org/playground/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.445Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.445Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.445Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:40.129Z","stars":21,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:58.497Z","stars":21,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:43:22.830Z","stars":22,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:03:19.775Z","stars":23,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-11T00:23:09.590Z","stars":23,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.445Z","stars":25,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["agnostic-ai is for developers and teams using more than one AI coding tool, or preparing to change tools. Write agents, skills, rules, hooks, and MCP configuration once; agnostic-ai sync turns those shared specifications (specs) into the files each tool reads. Skills provide task instructions, hooks run actions at chosen events, and MCP connects tools to external services. See Why agnostic-ai.","Each AI tool reads its instructions from different files. Kept by hand, those files fall out of step. agnostic-ai keeps one editable source in plain Markdown and YAML inside your repository. No account, no service.","Support spans Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Copilot, Kiro, and more. Each tool supports a different set of spec kinds; the target reference shows the exact paths."],"features":["Code review guidance in reviews/ reaches Cursor Bugbot, Codex, Goose, and Ellipsis. Ellipsis needs one reviewer named under x-ellipsis in a settings spec; sync then writes .ellipsis/code-review.yaml, and import ellipsis…","Claude handoff hooks follow the active checkout named by the event, including linked worktrees.","Shared skill names: doctor explains when a tool selects the home copy and project sync cannot change it. See shared names.","Manual-only skills keep their invocation flag in OpenCode V2. See support by tool.","Rules, agents, skills, and commands in one spec format. Kiro commands land in .kiro/prompts/ for CLI V3. import trae also reads shared .agents/skills/ folders, keeping .trae/skills/ first for duplicate names."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8ea7e951cebad4898d5493da4e59a146fb8cf9c922a9dea1df181e1f17a46d7c","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.582Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.582Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"agnostic-ai is for developers and teams using more than one AI coding tool, or preparing to change tools. Write agents, skills, rules, hooks, and MCP configuration once; agnostic-ai sync turns those shared specifications (specs) into the files each tool reads. Skills provide task instructions, hooks run actions at chosen events, and MCP connects tools to external services. See Why agnostic-ai.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No account, no service.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"8ea7e951cebad4898d5493da4e59a146fb8cf9c922a9dea1df181e1f17a46d7c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.583Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-15T12:58:52Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"htt